<title>CROATIA: World Bank grants Croatia $42 mln forestry loan.</title>
<headline>World Bank grants Croatia $42 mln forestry loan.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank has granted Croatia a $42 million loan for replanting and fire protection of forests in coastal regions, the national news agency HINA reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>It quoted the bank as saying the forestry project was aimed at helping the recovery of tourism on Croatia's coast. It would include planting of 5,800 hectares of new forests.</p>
<p>Total cost is estimated at $67.3 million, of which the World Bank pledged 62 percent.</p>
<p>The loan is repayable over 17 years with a five-year grace period at a &quot;standard rate.&quot; -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
